P	Test NAV_002 - Navigation Module Non-Functional Requirements
P	This test is intended to verify navigation module non-functional requirements:
P	NFR_014 - Map zoom limits
P	NFR_015 - Icon display clarity
P	NFR_016 - Zoom consistency
P	 
E	import display.TestSystem; import display.CNST; host.parent.centreMHDD.selectFormat(CNST.FORMAT.NAV);
PR	Confirm Navigation module is displayed in centre MHDD (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
P	 
P	Testing NFR_014 - Map zoom limits of 0.25x and 4.0x
PR	Press 'ZOOM' button to access zoom menu (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Press 'ZOOM OUT' button repeatedly until zoom stops changing (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Confirm zoom level stops at 0.25x (25% of original size) (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Press 'ZOOM IN' button repeatedly until zoom stops changing (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Confirm zoom level stops at 4.0x (400% of original size) (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Confirm zoom limits prevent further zooming beyond these boundaries (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
P	 
P	Testing NFR_015 - Icon display clarity
PR	Set zoom to minimum (0.25x) and confirm aircraft icon is visible and clear (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Set zoom to maximum (4.0x) and confirm aircraft icon is visible and clear (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Set zoom to default (1.0x) and confirm aircraft icon is visible and clear (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Confirm the red arrow representing the aircraft is clearly distinguishable at all zoom levels (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
P	 
P	Testing NFR_016 - Zoom consistency
PR	Set zoom to 2.0x (press ZOOM IN multiple times) (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Use arrow keys to fly aircraft in various directions (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Confirm zoom level remains constant at 2.0x while flying (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Change heading by 90 degrees and confirm zoom level is unchanged (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
PR	Confirm zoom induced by either zooming in or out varies by steady increments (0.25x per click) (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)
P	 
E	import display.TestSystem; import javafx.geometry.Point3D; host.parent.aircraftData.setVel(new Point3D(0.0, 1.0, 0.0));
E	import display.TestSystem; import javafx.geometry.Point3D; host.parent.aircraftData.setPos(new Point3D(200.0, -200.0, 0.0));
P	Aircraft position and velocity reset
P	 
PR	Confirm all navigation non-functional requirements have been adequately tested (GREEN - PASS, RED - FAIL)